{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0126oARk5AutojhtQJkZsREr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific reviewer guidelines and review form details are limited in the current search results. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Reviewer Information\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Review Evaluation Criteria\n\nBased on the CoRL 2024 guidance (which may be similar for 2026), submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nThe search results do not contain a complete CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines document or detailed review form. For the most current and complete reviewer guidelines and review form for CoRL 2026, I recommend:\n\n1. Visiting the official CoRL 2026 website at corl.org\n2. Checking the OpenReview platform at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference where submissions are handled\n3. Contacting the CoRL 2026 organizers directly through the official conference website\n\nThese sources would have the specific review form template and complete evaluation criteria for reviewers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b1a54116-c461-4e8a-8039-725147cd9263","uuid":"f2086cb0-d96c-488c-bb03-ba3dc822c33e","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:53:17.567Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0123jJ8z4E4QASU6jFRRSdcL","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific reviewer guidelines and review form details are limited in the current search results. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Reviewer Information\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n## Review Evaluation Criteria\n\nBased on the CoRL 2024 guidance (which may be similar for 2026), submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nThe search results do not contain a complete CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines document or detailed review form. For the most current and complete reviewer guidelines and review form for CoRL 2026, I recommend:\n\n1. Visiting the official CoRL 2026 website at corl.org\n2. Checking the OpenReview platform at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference where submissions are handled\n3. Contacting the CoRL 2026 organizers directly through the official conference website\n\nThese sources would have the specific review form template and complete evaluation criteria for reviewers."],"durationSeconds":5.754491365000002}}
