{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Nz7mceh2mh1PqufQXxV1En","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BZJ5EkD2B6wW3wBsv37oJu","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments Review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for a CoRL 2026 submission. Your focus is **Methods and Experiments**. Produce a thorough, independent review.\n\n## Venue: CoRL (Conference on Robot Learning)\n- Acceptance rate: ~30-35%\n- Review dimensions: Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance, Limitations\n- Overall score scale (1-10): 10=seminal/top5%, 9=strong accept/top15%, 8=clear accept/top50%, 7=good accept, 6=marginally above threshold, 5=marginally below threshold, 4=not good enough, 3=clear reject, 2=strong reject, 1=trivial/wrong\n- Confidence scale (1-5): 5=absolutely certain, 4=confident, 3=fairly confident, 2=willing to defend but not absolutely certain, 1=educated guess\n\n## Paper Summary\n**Title**: \"Token Pruning Catastrophically Fails on Pixel-Shuffle VLAs: Diagnosis and Recovery\"\n\n**Core claims**:\n1. Pixel-shuffle connectors (SmolVLA) catastrophically fail under ANY token pruning — 44.8% → 0% SR even removing just 5% of 128 tokens on LIBERO-Object\n2. Pure linear projection (π0) is immune — performance improves 2.4% even at 90% removal; CV=0.038\n3. CV-based zero-cost diagnostic predicts pruning tolerance from single forward pass (CV spectrum: 0.038 immune → 0.314 catastrophic)\n4. VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding, ~22M params, cross-attention) recovers pixel-shuffle VLAs from 0% → 60.1±1.3% at 75% compression; flat M-curve (M=16: 56.9% ≈ M=128: 58.0%)\n5. VTR fails on MLP-projector VLAs (OpenVLA): 0% SR across all M values — architecture-specific fix\n6. Pruning method confound: L2-norm vs random ~17pp systematic gap on OpenVLA\n7. Seed sensitivity: X-VLA k=0.7 shows 28pp variance across seeds (56.2% vs 28.0%)\n\n**Models tested**: SmolVLA (450M, pixel-shuffle, 128 tokens), X-VLA (880M, linear+BART 12L, 50 tokens), π0 (3.3B, pure linear, 256 tokens), OpenVLA (7B, 3-layer MLP, 256 tokens), OpenVLA-OFT (7B, same MLP)\n\n**Benchmark**: LIBERO-Object only (10 tasks, 50 episodes/task, 500 total). Wilson 95% CIs.\n\n**Key tables**:\n- Table 1: SmolVLA all pruning methods → 0% across all k values\n- Table 2: OpenVLA random vs L2-norm: systematic ~17pp gap at every k\n- Table 3: X-VLA cross-seed: k=0.7 seed42=56.2% vs seed44=28.0% (Δ=−28.2pp)\n- Table 4: SmolVLA VTR M-curve, 3-seed: all M values 54.5-62.0%, flat\n- Table 5: OpenVLA VTR all M values → 0% (action collapse)\n- Table 6: CV diagnostic summary across 5 models\n\n**VTR details**: Cross-attention with M learnable queries, VTC-only training (frozen LLM), 100K steps. SmolVLA 3-seed eval. Also tested MLP adapter (~22.14M params) achieving 63.4±2.6% at M=32 (p=0.15 vs cross-attention 60.1%), confirming re-encoding is the mechanism not specific architecture. Cross-suite generalization: Spatial 53.2%, Goal 56.4%.\n\n**π0 evaluation**: Offline only (normalized action-prediction loss), not closed-loop.\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (what was planned but may not all appear in paper)\nKey experiments that were planned:\n- OpenVLA L2-norm pruning full sweep (k=0.95/0.9/0.7/0.5/0.3) — ALL appear in paper Table 2\n- X-VLA cross-seed at k=0.7 (seed44) and k=0.9 (seed44) — appear in Table 3\n- OpenVLA cross-seed random pruning (seed43) at k=0.7 and k=0.5 — appear as text in Section 5.3\n- OpenVLA VTR (VTC-only) M=32/64/96/128 — appear in Table 5\n- SmolVLA VTR full M-sweep 3-seed — appear in Table 4\n- RoboFlamingo (Perceiver Resampler connector) — NOT completed, listed in Limitations as future work\n- SmolVLA VTR cross-suite generalization — mentioned in text\n\n## Your Review Focus: Methods and Experiments\n\nEvaluate:\n1. **Experimental methodology soundness**: Is the pruning protocol fair? Are baselines adequate? Is 500 episodes sufficient?\n2. **Statistical rigor**: Are CIs appropriate? Is 3-seed evaluation sufficient for VTR claims? Is single-seed okay for some results?\n3. **VTR method design**: Is the cross-attention re-encoding well-motivated? Is VTC-only training justified? Is 100K steps enough?\n4. **CV diagnostic validity**: Is CV of L2-norm a principled diagnostic? Only 4 data points on the CV spectrum — is this sufficient?\n5. **Confound analysis**: Is the L2-norm vs random comparison fair and well-executed?\n6. **Missing experiments**: What critical experiments are absent?\n7. **Reproducibility**: Is enough detail provided?\n8. **π0 offline-only evaluation**: How much does this weaken the claims?\n9. **Single benchmark (LIBERO-Object only)**: How limiting is this?\n\n## Output Format\n\n```\n## R1 Review: Methods and Experiments\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Strengths\n[Numbered list, specific and evidenced]\n\n### Weaknesses\n[Numbered list, specific and evidenced, with severity: major/minor]\n\n### Questions for Authors\n[Numbered list]\n\n### Missing Experiments\n[What would strengthen the paper]\n\n### Detailed Scores\n- Originality: X/10\n- Quality: X/10\n- Clarity: X/10\n- Significance: X/10\n- Relevance: X/10\n- Limitations acknowledgment: X/10\n\n### Overall Score: X/10\n### Confidence: X/5\n### Brief Justification\n[2-3 sentences]\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":633,"cache_read_input_tokens":54801,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":633},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b1a54116-c461-4e8a-8039-725147cd9263","uuid":"a923bdc3-0a5f-4d41-91f4-188820832cc8"}
