{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TjubvkV9GxtYufwCsNULeJ","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/analysis.tex-32-\\subsection{Limitations}\ndocs/paper/analysis.tex-33-\\label{sec:limitations}\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/analysis.tex-34-\ndocs/paper/analysis.tex:35:[Omitted long matching line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/analysis.tex-36-\ndocs/paper/analysis.tex-37-$\\pi_0$ evaluation is currently offline only; closed-loop results may reveal additional degradation not captured by single-step loss, as demonstrated by X-VLA's offline-to-closed-loop gap (Section~\\ref{sec:metric_disconnect}). X-VLA results at $k \\leq 0.2$ are based on 9 of 10 tasks (one task pending); final values may shift slightly.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/analysis.tex-38-\n--\ndocs/paper/discussion.tex-2-\\label{sec:discussion}\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/discussion.tex-3-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/discussion.tex-4-\\subsection{Disentangling Connector Design from Model Scale}\ndocs/paper/discussion.tex:5:\\label{sec:scale_confound}\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/discussion.tex-6-\ndocs/paper/discussion.tex:7:Our cross-architecture comparison confounds the vision connector design (pixel-shuffle vs.\\ MLP projector) with model scale (0.5B vs.\\ 7B parameters). A larger model has more capacity to absorb perturbations through its deeper and wider attention layers, raising the question of whether SmolVLA's cliff-edge reflects architectural fragility or simply insufficient model capacity.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/discussion.tex-8-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/discussion.tex-9-[Omitted long context line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/discussion.tex-10-\n--\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/discussion.tex-12-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/discussion.tex-13-[Omitted long context line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/discussion.tex-14-\ndocs/paper/discussion.tex:15:[Omitted long matching line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/discussion.tex-16-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/discussion.tex-17-[Omitted long context line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/discussion.tex-18-\n--\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/sections/results_draft.tex-83-[Omitted long context line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/sections/results_draft.tex-84-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/sections/results_draft.tex-85-\\paragraph{Architectural contrast.}\ndocs/paper/sections/results_draft.tex:86:[Omitted long matching line]\n--\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/sections/analysis_draft.tex-8-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/sections/analysis_draft.tex-9-[Omitted long context line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/sections/analysis_draft.tex-10-\ndocs/paper/sections/analysis_draft.tex:11:[Omitted long matching line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/sections/analysis_draft.tex-12-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/sections/analysis_draft.tex-13-\\subsection{Attention Distribution as a Compressibility Predictor}\ndocs/paper/sections/analysis_draft.tex-14-\\label{sec:attention_distribution}\n--\ndocs/paper/background.tex-55-Unlike SmolVLA's pixel-shuffle connector, OpenVLA maps vision encoder outputs to the language model through a three-layer MLP projector (GELU activations) that processes each patch token independently. This design preserves per-token independence: the representation of one token carries no implicit dependency on neighboring tokens' presence. The projector produces 256 vision tokens that maintain a one-to-one correspondence with spatial patch locations.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/background.tex-56-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/background.tex-57-\\paragraph{Architectural contrast.}\ndocs/paper/background.tex:58:The key difference for compressibility is the connector design. SmolVLA's pixel-shuffle folds 16 patches into each token, creating dense, entangled representations where removing one token eliminates a $4 \\times 4$ spatial region. OpenVLA's MLP projector preserves patch-level granularity, so removing one token discards approximately $1/256$ of the visual field. Model scale (0.5B vs.\\ 7B) is a confound that we discuss in Section~\\ref{sec:discussion}.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/background.tex-59-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/background.tex-60-\\subsection{LIBERO Benchmark}\ndocs/paper/background.tex-61-\\label{sec:libero_bench}\n--\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/experimental_setup.tex-31-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/experimental_setup.tex-32-[Omitted long context line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/experimental_setup.tex-33-\ndocs/paper/experimental_setup.tex:34:[Omitted long matching line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/experimental_setup.tex-35-\ndocs/paper/experimental_setup.tex-36-Two metrics characterize each model's vision token structure from a single forward pass on task-relevant frames. \\emph{Attention entropy ratio}: normalized Shannon entropy of attention weights over vision tokens, where low entropy indicates concentrated attention on a few tokens. \\emph{Token importance CV}: coefficient of variation of L2 norms across vision tokens, where high CV signals heterogeneous importance distribution.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/experimental_setup.tex-37-\n--\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/results.tex-43-\ndocs/paper/results.tex-44-$\\pi_0$~\\cite{black2024pi0} (3.3B, 256 tokens, linear projection) is evaluated via offline normalized L1 action loss.\\footnote{Offline action loss measures single-step prediction quality; closed-loop evaluation may reveal additional degradation. X-VLA's offline-to-closed-loop gap (Section~\\ref{sec:metric_disconnect}) underscores the need for live verification.} At $k{=}0.1$, the loss is 0.976---a 2.4\\% \\emph{improvement} over the unpruned baseline. At $k{=}0.5$ the loss remains 0.983.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/results.tex-45-\ndocs/paper/results.tex:46:[Omitted long matching line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/results.tex-47-\ndocs/paper/results.tex-48-\\subsection{VTR: Re-Encoding Overcomes Cliff-Edge}\ndocs/paper/results.tex-49-\\label{sec:smart_compress_results}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BZJ5EkD2B6wW3wBsv37oJu","session_id":"b1a54116-c461-4e8a-8039-725147cd9263","uuid":"3f6b6ddf-e4a4-491d-a794-c075805df963","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:55:24.472Z"}
