{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W6CTGdtpuV9b2Qg8UWVEZe","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/analysis.tex-6-\ndocs/paper/analysis.tex-7-The $\\pi_0$--OpenVLA controlled comparison (Section~\\ref{sec:taxonomy_overview}) isolates the connector as causal: 63\\,pp gap at $k{=}0.1$ with token count and encoder held constant. The mechanism lies in how each connector creates different token independence structures.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/analysis.tex-8-\ndocs/paper/analysis.tex:9:[Omitted long matching line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/analysis.tex-10-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/analysis.tex-11-[Omitted long context line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/analysis.tex-12-\n--\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/results.tex-43-\ndocs/paper/results.tex-44-$\\pi_0$~\\cite{black2024pi0} (3.3B, 256 tokens, linear projection) is evaluated via offline normalized L1 action loss.\\footnote{Offline action loss measures single-step prediction quality; closed-loop evaluation may reveal additional degradation. X-VLA's offline-to-closed-loop gap (Section~\\ref{sec:metric_disconnect}) underscores the need for live verification.} At $k{=}0.1$, the loss is 0.976---a 2.4\\% \\emph{improvement} over the unpruned baseline. At $k{=}0.5$ the loss remains 0.983.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/docs/paper/results.tex-45-\ndocs/paper/results.tex:46:[Omitted long matching line]\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/impo